        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0744" n="1704" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1704"/>

                <head>No. 13.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-12-01"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 1, 1888</date>.
                        (Received December 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 858.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith for
                    your information an extract from the Times newspaper of 27th ultimo, containing
                    a question asked by Mr. Gourley in the House of Commons and answered by Sir
                    James Fergusson, under secretary of state for foreign affairs, with respect to
                    the appointment of a new minister to the United States. I also inclose a leader
                    from the Daily News on the subject.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. J. Phelps.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d436-a1.xml" xpointer="d436-a1"/>
